  "registerId": "GRIT-RED-PATTERNS",
  "status": "DRAFT_FOR_REVIEW",
  "note": "Tiny patterns for urgent events. A hit is a RED candidate: a prompt for R&A to check, not RED. RED is confirmed only by a named R&A confirmer who names the trigger in 'triggers' that happened to the business (URS methodology, section 14). Tiny patterns for urgent events. A hit drafts an email for a named person to send or dismiss. Nothing is sent automatically. A pattern must hit the title or the lead, and the event must be corroborated by a second outlet or carried by a HIGH-rated registered source. A pattern in a sentence that forecasts, assesses, or rehearses the event (the rule's excludeInSentence words) does not count: 'invasion of Taiwan unlikely before 2028' is not an invasion.",
